# Data fetching performance (Volvo OFV)

## Server first

- Pages in `src/app/(app)/` are Server Components — fetch data in the page or tab panel, pass props down.
- Add `"use client"` only for filters, charts (Recharts), dialogs, and navigation state.

## Tab-scoped loading

- Gate expensive work by active tab (see `getRegistrationsPageData` + `loadOverview` / `loadDetaljer` / `loadKjopere`).
- New tabs with heavy data get their own loader (`getRegionTabData`, `getMarkedTabData`) in a dedicated panel component.

## Supabase calls

- Batch independent reads with `Promise.all` — but limit total RPC count per page load.
- List queries: explicit column list + `.range()` pagination — never `select('*')` for tables.
- Counts: `{ count: 'exact', head: true }` only when the UI needs them; avoid duplicate counts.
- Aggregations: `.rpc('reg_summary_by_*')` / `.rpc('pop_summary_by_*')`, not client-side reduce.

## Filters and state

- URL filters via `nuqs` in client filter components; server pages read `searchParams`.
- Saved report views store minimal config — mirror URL filter fields in `src/lib/report-views/config.ts`.

## Example

```typescript
// ✅ Tab-gated fetch
const loadOverview = tab === "oversikt";
const monthlyRes = loadOverview
  ? rpcClient.rpc("reg_summary_by_month", args)
  : Promise.resolve({ data: [], error: null });

// ❌ Fetch all tab data on every request
const [region, marked, buyers, rows] = await Promise.all([...]);
```

